{"text": " "}, {"text": "reuptake"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inhibitors"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-26697", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Discontinuation symptoms are experienced due to receptor adaptation or receptor rebound after stopping of antidepressants. It can be avoided or reduced by slowly tapering the drug over at least 4 weeks. Symptoms include flu-like symptoms, ‘shock- like” sensations, dizziness exacerbated by movement, insomnia, vivid dreaming and irritability, problems with concentration, and memory or movement disorders.", "runs": [{"text": "Discontinuation symptoms are experienced due to receptor adaptation or receptor rebound after stopping of antidepressants. It can be avoided or reduced by slowly tapering the drug over at least 4 weeks. Symptoms include flu-like symptoms, ‘shock- like” sensations, dizziness exacerbated by movement, insomnia, vivid dreaming and irritability, problems with concentration, and memory or movement disorders."}]}, {"id": "body-26698", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is managed by reintroduction of the SSRI and slower tapering of the dose.", "runs": [{"text": "It"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "managed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reintroduction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "SSRI"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "slower"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "tapering"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose."}]}, {"id": "body-26699-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Note: Fluoxetine seldom causes discontinuation symptoms because of its long half-life.", "runs": [{"text": "Note:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Fluoxetine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "seldom"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "causes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "discontinuation"},